2026-05-25  Sigitas Tolušis <sigitas@vtex.lt>

	* xdvips.c: bump VTEX_VERSION to 2026.05.25.

	* glyphlist_table.lua, glyphlist_table.h: extend glyph-to-Unicode
	table with ~360 entries from the newtx/newpx (ntx) and luaotf glyph
	sets: blackboard-bold letters (bbA-bbZ, bba-bbz), math arrows and
	brackets, accent combiners (arcwide*, tilde*, bar*), and
	miscellaneous symbols.  Normalise entry order to case-sensitive
	alphabetical (uppercase before lowercase) throughout.

	* Build/Dockerfile, Build/builder.sh, Build/Makefile: add
	Docker-based Linux (x86-64) build infrastructure.  The container
	runs as the host user to prevent ownership changes in the source
	tree; output goes into Build/source/Work-linux/.

	* configure.ac, configure: fix zziplib AX_PREFIX_CONFIG_H macro
	for autoconf 2.73 where $as_echo is not yet defined at the point
	the macro expands.

	* configure.ac, Makefile.am: refactor --with-system-libjpeg and
	--with-system-libtiff to use the standard KPSE macro infrastructure
	(kpse_try_pkg / kpse_add_flags) for consistency with the rest of
	the TeX Live build system.

2026-05-20  Sigitas Tolušis <sigitas@vtex.lt>

	* Makefile.am, Makefile.in: change LIBJPEG_LIBS/LIBTIFF_LIBS from
	hardcoded libjpeg.a/libtiff.a to @LIBJPEG_BUILT@/@LIBTIFF_BUILT@
	so that bundled archives are not built as xdvipsk dependencies when
	system libraries are selected via --with-system-libjpeg/libtiff.
	* graphlib/loadJPEG.cpp: guard local static jpeg_read_icc_profile
	definition with #ifndef LIBJPEG_TURBO_VERSION_NUMBER so it is not
	compiled when using libjpeg-turbo, which already declares the
	function in its public jpeglib.h.

	* Makefile.am, Makefile.in: add tif_unix.c (Unix) / tif_win32.c
	(Windows cross) to libtiff_a_SOURCES so the bundled libtiff provides
	_TIFFmalloc, _TIFFfree, _TIFFwarningHandler etc. that loadTIFF.cpp
	no longer defines; add compile rules and am__append_3 conditional.
	* graphlib/loadJPEG.cpp: add #include <stddef.h>/<stdio.h> before
	extern "C" block (needed by bundled jpeglib.h for size_t/FILE);
	restore HAVE_BOOLEAN guard (C++ mode makes jmorecfg.h define boolean
	as enum otherwise, conflicting with bitmap.h int macros TRUE/FALSE).
	* thirdparty/libtiff/libtiff-src/tif_config.h: define HAVE_UNISTD_H
	and HAVE_SYS_TYPES_H so tif_unix.c can include <unistd.h>.

